# Normalize line endings in the index so text sources are byte-identical across
# platforms. Several tests read real sources and stylesheets through Vite's
# `?raw` suffix and assert on multi-line text. With a per-machine
# `core.autocrlf=true` those imports yield CRLF on Windows checkouts and the
# assertions fail for a reason unrelated to the code (observed on this repo:
# src/ui/compare/CounterfactualCompareStyles.test.ts and
# src/ui/analysis/AnalysisPanel.test.tsx fail only under CRLF).
* text=auto

# Text that tests and reproducible-identity tooling read verbatim must always be
# LF in the working tree, independent of any contributor's autocrlf setting.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never normalize binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
